# Claude Code Custom Instructions for Adversarial Plate Repository

## Development Workflow
- **All changes MUST be committed and pushed** to the repository after completion
- User will pull changes on their compute machine and run code there
- Do not run code locally on this development machine

## Code Editing Best Practices
- Prefer using the Read and Edit tools for file operations
- Only use bash commands (sed, awk, cat) as a last resort
- Read a file first before editing to ensure proper context
- Use Edit tool for replacements, Write tool for new files

## Commits
- Include descriptive commit messages that explain the "why"
- Always include Co-Authored-By footer: `Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`
